      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>You can view both general networking metrics and OVN-Kubernetes metrics from the dashboard.</p>
      <p>To view general networking metrics, select <strong>Networking/Linux Subsystem Stats</strong> from the <strong>Dashboards</strong> drop-down list. You can view the following networking metrics from the dashboard: <strong>Network Utilisation</strong>, <strong>Network Saturation</strong>, and <strong>Network Errors</strong>.</p>
      <p>To view OVN-Kubernetes metrics select <strong>Networking/Infrastructure</strong> from the <strong>Dashboards</strong> drop-down list. You can view the following OVN-Kubernetes metrics: <strong>Networking Configuration</strong>, <strong>TCP Latency Probes</strong>, <strong>Control Plane Resources</strong>, and <strong>Worker Resources</strong>.</p>
      </dd>
      <dt class="font-semibold">Ingress Operator dashboard</dt>
      <dd class="ml-6 text-muted-foreground">
      <p>You can view networking metrics handled by the Ingress Operator from the dashboard. This includes metrics like the following:</p>
      <ul>
      <li>Incoming and outgoing bandwidth</li>
      <li>HTTP error rates</li>
      <li>HTTP server response latency</li>
      </ul>
